"""Real-world calibration corpus: Indian-market skincare products.

Used to check that the engine's scores are defensible against products people
actually buy, rather than only against synthetic ideal/terrible formulas.

INCI lists are reconstructed from public product listings and are approximate -
minor ingredients may be missing or ordered slightly differently. That is
adequate here, because this corpus exists to surface STRUCTURAL problems
(category logic, unreachable ceilings, inverted rankings, nonsense messaging),
which do not depend on exact ingredient order.

`expect` is a rough band a knowledgeable reviewer would place the product in,
used to flag outliers for human review. It is a sanity check, not ground truth.
"""

